    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_1_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "The impact of Cochrane Reviews that apply network meta-analysis in clinical guidelines: A systematic review",
      "reason": "The report title explicitly includes the wording “A systematic review,” identifying it as a systematic review."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_1_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "The impact of Cochrane Reviews that apply network meta-analysis in clinical guidelines",
      "reason": "The title provides key objective information by specifying the focus: the “impact” of Cochrane Reviews that apply network meta-analysis when used in clinical guidelines."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_1_e3",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "The impact of Cochrane Reviews that apply network meta-analysis in clinical guidelines: A systematic review",
      "reason": "The title includes relevant supplementary information about the analysis method context (“network meta-analysis”) but does not indicate other items such as update status/living status or included study designs."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 74
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_3",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "Nevertheless, Cochrane Reviews have been greatly under-utilised in guidelines and recommendations are often based on lowerlevel evidence or expert consensus because of limitations regarding familiarity, awareness, usefulness, access, and time [12-21].",
      "reason": "The introduction describes gaps in current knowledge/use in guidelines (under-utilisation and reasons), but it does not explicitly articulate “important uncertainties” in the sense of unresolved questions needing clarification."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "Yet, if a review does not provide evidence to strengthen or change recommendations or is not used by guideline developers, the review could potentially have very limited impact on healthcare and may be considered a poor use of time, funds, and resources.",
      "reason": "The rationale explains why conducting the review matters: guideline uptake affects healthcare impact and resource use."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "Limited research has explored the use of NMAs to inform guidelines [38]. Lunny et al summarised how often NMAs and PW-MAs support recommendations in a sample of 50 guidelines [15]. Our article is the first to systematically search for reviews and summarise their citation in guidelines, and to explore the citation of reviews in depth.",
      "reason": "When prior similar work exists (e.g., Lunny et al.), the need for this review is explained and previous research is cited; the manuscript also claims novelty relative to prior work."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No proposed mechanism of action is described for the intervention effects (no brief mechanism is provided in the retrieved introduction/background evidence)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The retrieved evidence does not include a logic model showing hypothesised relationships between intervention components and outcomes."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 72
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_4",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "We aimed to summarise which, when, where, who, and why Cochrane Reviews that applied NMA were cited in guidelines; and to compare the citation of NMA reviews in guidelines with PW-MA reviews.",
      "reason": "The review objective(s) are explicitly stated (“We aimed to…”), but the statement is not presented using a specific question-formulation framework (e.g., PICO-style for objectives), so it is only partially met."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e2",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "We aimed to summarise which, when, where, who, and why Cochrane Reviews that applied NMA were cited in guidelines; and to compare the citation of NMA reviews in guidelines with PW-MA reviews.",
      "reason": "This is a review of how Cochrane reviews are cited in clinical guidelines (citation/uptake), not a review of intervention effects where planned intervention comparisons would be stated using PICO or a variant."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 78
}

{
